+# Bun migration
+
+Use Bun 1.4.4. Install development dependencies reproducibly with
+`bun install --frozen-lockfile`.
+
+## Commands
+
+- `bun run run -- <operation> <path> [text]` runs the CLI. Supported operations
+  remain `new`, `replace`, `read`, `missing`, `list`, and `child`.
+- `bun run check` preserves the previous checking entry point.
+- `bun run typecheck` runs TypeScript 6.0.3 with `strict: true` and no emission,
+  covering application sources and regression tests. Bun execution alone does
+  not typecheck TypeScript.
+- `bun test` runs the added regression tests.
+
+No serve or build tasks existed. No production dependencies existed. The new
+exact development dependencies are TypeScript 6.0.3 and Bun types 1.4.4; bun.lock
+also pins their transitive dependencies. Deno configuration and execution have
+been removed.
+
+## Preserved behavior
+
+The CLI uses Node filesystem APIs provided by Bun. Exclusive creation uses `wx`
+so existing files cannot be overwritten; replace creates or truncates a file.
+Text reads return JSON-encoded UTF-8 text. Missing-file detection catches only
+`ENOENT`; other read errors still fail. Listings sort regular file names and
+exclude directories and symbolic links. The child runs with the same Bun
+executable as its parent, using a filesystem path derived from the module URL.
+Both output streams are drained concurrently and fully, and its exit code 7 is
+reported in the parent's JSON output without failing the parent.
+
+## Intentional runtime and security differences
+
+Bun does not implement Deno's permission sandbox. The previous main command
+explicitly allowed read/write/process execution, while other capabilities such
+as environment and network access remained restricted. Bun and spawned Bun
+children inherit the host user's ordinary permissions, including filesystem,
+environment, and network access. The previous child had no Deno permission
+flags. Use operating-system isolation when running untrusted code or inputs;
+this migration does not provide a replacement capability sandbox.
+
+Filesystem failures now use Node error codes rather than Deno error classes.
+Uncaught-error messages, stack traces, and package task banners differ by
+runtime; failure remains nonzero. The public successful output and file side
+effects are preserved.
+
+## Validation
+
+On the supplied Bun 1.4.4 executable: `bun run typecheck`, `bun run check`,
+`bun test` (6 passing tests, 18 assertions), and `bun install --frozen-lockfile`
+passed. A disposable comparison against the supplied Deno baseline matched all
+10 observations for stdout, exit status, and preserved file contents, including
+both complete 120,001-byte child streams. Tests cover exclusive creation,
+UTF-8/JSON text, default empty text, replacement truncation and creation,
+missing-file handling and other errors, sorted file-only listings, child output,
+and unknown operations.
+
+Validation was on macOS; other operating systems and adversarial concurrent
+filesystem changes were not separately tested. Formatting/lint replacement is
+outside this migration's scope.
